From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdiplus: GDI records in EMF-only and EMF+ dual metafiles

Everything drawn on a recorded metafile now also goes into its GDI half:
an EMF-only recording was empty (and DrawLine/DrawPath and the other
drawing calls failed with NotImplemented), an EMF+ dual one carried only
the EMF+ records, so a program that plays GDI only (PlayEnhMetaFile, the
clipboard) saw nothing. A graphics object on the recording device context
draws the GDI records with the world transform, page unit and scale, clip
and quality settings of the program's graphics object: fills and strokes of
rectangles, ellipses, arcs, pies, paths and regions, images, driver
strings and Clear. GDI+ plays a dual file's EMF+ records only, so nothing
is drawn twice. A recorded EMF-only metafile reports an EMF+ version.
Removes the todo_wine marks of the version and DrawLine checks; the
EMF-only draw test checks the records both we and Windows write, in order
(Windows writes a single polyline, we stroke a path: still a todo).
